#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:3
msgid "Standalone Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:5
msgid ""
"Install an app under a Python interpreter downloaded from `python-build-"
"standalone <https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone>`_ instead "
"of the system one. Reach for this when the system Python lacks the version "
"you need, or when a distro patched its Python in ways that break the app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:11
msgid "How pipx decides"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:13
msgid ""
"``--fetch-python`` (or ``PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON``) sets the policy. With "
"``missing``, pipx downloads only when no local interpreter satisfies the "
"app's ``requires-python``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:35
msgid ""
"Naming ``--python`` yourself keeps the last word: pipx uses the interpreter "
"you named and reports it, rather than overriding you when the package "
"rejects it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:40
msgid "Set the policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:46
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:47
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:48
msgid "``never``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:49
msgid ""
"Default. Never download; use interpreters from ``PATH`` or the ``py`` "
"launcher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:50
msgid "``missing``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:51
msgid "Look locally first; download when the requested version is not found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:52
msgid "``always``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:53
msgid ""
"Skip the local search and use a standalone build for the requested version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:55
msgid ""
"$ pipx install --python 3.13 --fetch-python=missing my-package\n"
"$ pipx install --python 3.13 --fetch-python=always my-package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:60
msgid "Set it for the whole shell session with the environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:62
msgid ""
"$ export PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON=missing\n"
"$ pipx install --python 3.13 my-package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:67
msgid ""
"Reach for ``always`` in CI runs that should not depend on the runner's "
"Python, on distros that strip modules like ``tkinter`` or ``lzma``, or on "
"air-gapped hosts with a populated standalone cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:72
msgid "Manage cached interpreters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:74
msgid ""
"pipx unpacks each interpreter into its standalone cache. Manage them with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:76
msgid ""
"$ pipx interpreter list\n"
"$ pipx interpreter prune\n"
"$ pipx interpreter upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:84
msgid ""
"``--fetch-missing-python`` and ``PIPX_FETCH_MISSING_PYTHON`` still work but "
"are deprecated aliases for ``--fetch-python=missing`` / "
"``PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON=missing``. pipx errors if you set both "
"``PIPX_FETCH_MISSING_PYTHON`` and ``PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:90
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:92
msgid "$ pipx list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:96
msgid ""
"The environment lists the interpreter version pipx settled on. For how pipx "
"resolves interpreters, see :doc:`../explanation/how-pipx-works`."
msgstr ""
